Minato's patch to frameworks/base's media/java/android/media/MediaPlayer.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0),
ADR-0060 e2e1: the static initializer loads no libmedia_jni, a URL takes no http service, and three parameters lose
MediaDrm's annotations.

Why: as MediaCodec's and MediaExtractor's (mediacodec-without-media-jni.patch), its natives are libandroid_runtime's
(framework/native/android_runtime/android_media_MediaPlayer.cpp), registered when the process starts. Minato has no
http service for media (MediaHTTPService is not taken): the natives check the app's INTERNET permission and its
network security config for an http or https URL, as MediaPlayerService and MediaHTTPConnection do, and the host's
player fetches it. MediaDrm is the managers' generated stand-in, which has no KeyType or StringProperty annotation.

--- a/media/java/android/media/MediaPlayer.java
+++ b/media/java/android/media/MediaPlayer.java
@@ -617,8 +617,7 @@
     public static final boolean BYPASS_METADATA_FILTER = false;
 
     static {
-        System.loadLibrary("media_jni");
-        native_init();
+        native_init();  // Minato: the natives are libandroid_runtime's, registered at the start, no media_jni
     }
 
     private final static String TAG = "MediaPlayer";
@@ -1223,7 +1222,7 @@
         } else if (scheme != null) {
             // handle non-file sources
             nativeSetDataSource(
-                MediaHTTPService.createHttpServiceBinderIfNecessary(path, cookies),
+                null /* Minato: no http service, MediaHTTPService.createHttpServiceBinderIfNecessary(path, cookies) */,
                 path,
                 keys,
                 values);
@@ -5160,7 +5159,7 @@
      */
     @NonNull
     public MediaDrm.KeyRequest getKeyRequest(@Nullable byte[] keySetId, @Nullable byte[] initData,
-            @Nullable String mimeType, @MediaDrm.KeyType int keyType,
+            @Nullable String mimeType, /* Minato: @MediaDrm.KeyType */ int keyType,
             @Nullable Map<String, String> optionalParameters)
             throws NoDrmSchemeException
     {
@@ -5304,7 +5303,7 @@
      * {@link MediaDrm#PROPERTY_DESCRIPTION}, {@link MediaDrm#PROPERTY_ALGORITHMS}
      */
     @NonNull
-    public String getDrmPropertyString(@NonNull @MediaDrm.StringProperty String propertyName)
+    public String getDrmPropertyString(@NonNull /* Minato: @MediaDrm.StringProperty */ String propertyName)
             throws NoDrmSchemeException
     {
         Log.v(TAG, "getDrmPropertyString: propertyName: " + propertyName);
@@ -5341,7 +5340,7 @@
